    description: "Re-measurement during WI-kipod (2026-07-01). WI-kazob (done) added module docstrings to file-kind Symbols at construction, and the analyzer DOES emit them: analyze_python(/tmp/kipod_probe) returns kind='file' symbols mod_a.py docstring='Module A: provides the greeting primitives...' and mod_b.py docstring='Module B: the entrypoint...'. But the SERIALIZED behavior map drops them: mod_a.py's file node is ABSENT entirely, and mod_b.py's file node survives (it is the src of an import edge) but its docstring is None. So 0 file-kind nodes carry a module summary in the emitted map despite WI-kazob's construction-side fix.\\n\\nTwo distinct losses: (1) file nodes with no incident edges appear to be pruned as orphans (mod_a.py has classes/functions but no file-level edge -> gone); (2) surviving file nodes lose their docstring somewhere between analyzer output and serialization. create_boundary_nodes (ir.py ~1247-1388) is NOT the culprit -- it only synthesizes kind='external_symbol' nodes for dangling external ids, not first-party file nodes. Suspects: orphan-node pruning + INV-hojus dual-symbol (kind='module' vs kind='file') reconciliation, and/or finalize.\\n\\nRepro: build /tmp/kipod_probe with two py files each having a module docstring; run 'hypergumbo run'; compare analyze_python() file-node docstrings (present) vs bm.json file-node docstrings (None / node absent).\\n\\nImpact: blocks sketch 'Source Files' section from ever showing module summaries (WI-kipod wires the render-when-present display, but the data never arrives). Structural: likely affects every language's file-anchor nodes, not just Python. Related: WI-kazob (done, construction-side), WI-dagif (done, missing file-anchor nodes for 13 files), WI-kipod (display)."  # e5e7
    fields: {}  # e5e7
