  message: "Withdrawn — not a real defect. The repro was run against the STALE pipx binary at /home/jgstern_agent/.local/bin/hypergumbo (a pre-WI-kazob 6.1.0 build), which predates this session's Phase 1 file-node-docstring work and so emitted 0 file-node docstrings — exactly the pre-WI-kazob state. Re-measured with the EDITABLE dev install (.venv/bin/hypergumbo = current working tree): file-anchor docstrings are present end-to-end. Behavioral evidence: (1) probe /tmp/kipod_probe map — both mod_a.py and mod_b.py file nodes carry their module docstrings, mod_a.py's file node is NOT pruned; (2) real target packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker — 34/34 file-kind nodes carry docstrings (e.g. store.py -> 'Store for the hypergumbo tracker — YAML I/O, compile, CRUD, Lamport clock.'). This matches WI-kazob's own closure evidence (845/908 file nodes). The filing contradicted WI-kazob and should have been caught as a stale-binary measurement error. Lesson: verify CLI behavior with .venv/bin/hypergumbo (which `which hypergumbo` resolves to), never the pipx .local/bin copy."  # 6089
